From: Goby private toolchain maintainers
Subject: [PRIVATE PATCH] avfilter/libplacebo: require audited per-frame Dolby Vision
Upstream-base: FFmpeg n9.0.1 (bf1b838f2ab88b4f8fd83443325c782ea0e0f7fa)
Upstream-source: https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n9.0.1/libavfilter/vf_libplacebo.c
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later; the upstream source license header is unchanged.

Add opt-in strict Dolby Vision processing for HEVC profiles 5, 7 and 8.
Fail closed on missing/unsupported frame metadata, profile mismatches and FEL.
Normalize a private metadata copy only for verified zero-residual profile 7
MEL, preserving every original reshaping curve, color matrix and extension.
Require libplacebo to report that it actually mapped the validated metadata.

This private patch is pinned to FFmpeg n9.0.1 and libplacebo 7.351.0.
See README.md in this patch directory for provenance and verification scope.

